From: aleks2 (H37-c5)
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] stop safely when the host gives no data directory

GetRandomizerPath() built a std::filesystem::path from the null pointer HostService::data_dir
leaves behind when it fails, after calling HostService::fail -- which returns. H37-c4 on Switch
("Failed to get data directory (1)") then crashed in the next instruction, before the loader's
Disable at the next safe point. The five path functions now return std::optional: nullopt when
the host refuses (or reports OK with a null or empty path), fail() is called once, and every
caller stops what it was doing (config in memory only, no seed/preset listing, no generation, no
file written) instead of writing to the current directory. Randomizer::GenerateTrackerWorld() (generator/randomizer.cpp) stops too: it
built the anti-spoiler log path from the seeds path and would not compile against the optional. data_dir.hpp holds the lookup so a host
test can run it against a stub host.
---
diff --git a/src/data_dir.hpp b/src/data_dir.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d87732c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/data_dir.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+#pragma once
+
+// aleks2 (H37-c5): the mod's persistent directory as the host reports it, with nothing assumed.
+// HostService::data_dir can fail (H37-c4 on Switch: "Failed to get data directory (1)") and
+// HostService::fail returns to its caller -- it marks the mod failed, the loader disables it at the next
+// safe point, and the code that asked keeps running until it returns. So a failed lookup must end in
+// "no path", never in a path built from the null pointer data_dir leaves in *out.
+
+#include <filesystem>
+#include <optional>
+
+#include <mods/svc/host.h>
+
+namespace randomizer::paths {
+
+// nullopt when the host refuses, or reports MOD_OK with no or an empty path.
+inline std::optional<std::filesystem::path> ResolveDataDir(const HostService* host, ModContext* ctx) {
+    if (host == nullptr || host->data_dir == nullptr) {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    const char* dataDir = nullptr;
+    if (host->data_dir(ctx, &dataDir) != MOD_OK || dataDir == nullptr || dataDir[0] == '\0') {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    return std::filesystem::path(reinterpret_cast<const char8_t*>(dataDir));
+}
+
+}  // namespace randomizer::paths
